{
  "header": [
    "ECP-R3-P1 — rs-conformance's probe for root-entity content_hash validation.",
    "",
    "⛔⭐ THIS ITEM DISAGREES WITH ITS OWN REQUIREMENT FILE ABOUT WHETHER A CODE IS PINNED, AND THE",
    "DISAGREEMENT IS EMITTED RATHER THAN RESOLVED HERE. ECP-R3's `reading` concludes \"ANY status",
    "and code satisfies this file; the FRAME is what is asserted\", arguing that §4.11's cause",
    "table has no root-hash row \"by arch's deliberate design\" and that §1.8/§7.2 assign no code.",
    "Read against the snapshot THAT FILE ITSELF DECLARES, the argument does not hold — see the",
    "`contested` block. The probe therefore SCORES the half both readings share (the frame",
    "obligation) and WITNESSES the (status, code) with the contested evaluation attached.",
    "",
    "Prohibition 2: we state what the spec requires, we do not decide it. Unilaterally failing the",
    "cohort on a code the requirement file says is unpinned would be authoring the specification;",
    "silently adopting the file's conclusion against the pinned text would be the check-bug horn of",
    "our own three-way table. Routing it is the third option and it is the right one."
  ],

  "id": "ECP-R3-P1",
  "author": "rs-conformance",
  "class": "validate-peer check",
  "class_basis": [
    "GUIDE-CONFORMANCE §7.0's first class: behavioral, over the wire, against a running peer. The",
    "input is one §5.1 frame and the observation is the peer's answer on the same connection.",
    "§6.5 places `Validate root entity hash` in the inbound dispatch chain, which is a wire path."
  ],
  "drives": [
    "entity-core-protocol/ECP-R3"
  ],
  "surface": "wire",
  "status": "draft",
  "snapshot": "entity-core-protocol/v0.8.2.26",

  "preconditions": {
    "posture": "pre-handshake-floor",
    "connection_state": "not_established",
    "grants": "none — §4.2 makes `system/protocol/connect` the sole pre-authorized path in any connection state",
    "identities": "none — §3.2 exempts the connection path from `author` and `capability`, and no signature is sent",
    "connection_reuse": "none; a fresh TCP connection per arm",
    "why_a_hello_is_the_vehicle": [
      "A hello needs no author, no capability and no signature, so a refusal of a MIS-HASHED hello",
      "can only be about the hash, and an answered one proves the hash was not checked. No posture",
      "can be blamed for either outcome. This is the requirement file's own argument and it",
      "survives contact with §4.2."
    ]
  },

  "arm": [
    {
      "name": "conformant_coded_refusal_of_a_mis_hashed_root",
      "kind": "conformant",
      "given": "a fresh TCP connection, no frames previously sent on it",
      "why": [
        "§1.8 item 1: \"Compute expected hash from `{type, data}`, compare with `content_hash`,",
        "reject on mismatch.\" §7.2 gives the algorithm as NORMATIVE and ends in REJECT. §6.5 places",
        "it first after decode. ENTITY-CBOR-ENCODING §5.2: \"never trust a claimed hash without",
        "verification.\"",
        "",
        "THE REFUSAL'S SHAPE is §4.11's, and 0.8.2.26 is what makes §4.11 reach this cause: \"The",
        "table assigns CODES; it does not define the CLASS [MUST]. Membership is decided by the",
        "boundary in this section's first sentence ... and EVERY MEMBER CARRIES THE FRAME",
        "OBLIGATION whether or not its cause has a row here.\" A mis-hashed root hello is refused",
        "before the frame becomes an admitted request. It is a member.",
        "",
        "THE DEFECT IS ONE BIT, on purpose. A structurally odd hash could plausibly be refused by a",
        "length check or a format-code check, and those are different rows; a single flipped bit in",
        "the digest leaves the field the right width under the right format code, so the only thing",
        "that can refuse it is the comparison."
      ],
      "step": [
        {
          "op": "send_frame",
          "detail": "envelope { root: EXECUTE(uri=`system/protocol/connect`, operation=`hello`, params=hello per §3.8) } with the ROOT entity's carried content_hash differing from SHA-256(ECF({type,data})) by one bit; everything else canonical, correctly framed, no tag, no `included`"
        },
        {
          "op": "read_frame",
          "detail": "one answer"
        }
      ],
      "accept": [
        {
          "outcome": "coded_response",
          "detail": "a coded EXECUTE_RESPONSE refusal on the wire. ⚠ SCORED ON THE FRAME ONLY — the (status, code) is witnessed and evaluated under `contested`, not scored."
        }
      ],
      "refuse": [
        {
          "outcome": "hello_answered",
          "detail": "THE FAILURE THE ROW EXISTS FOR: a 2xx means the root was processed without its hash being validated"
        },
        {
          "outcome": "silent_drop",
          "detail": "§4.11's FIRST named failure. SCORED SEPARATELY from the bare close."
        },
        {
          "outcome": "bare_close",
          "detail": "§4.11's SECOND named failure. SCORED SEPARATELY. ⛔ This outcome was ACCEPTED by a sibling instrument until 2026-09-16 (F77), which is why it is spelled out as its own refuse row rather than folded into a generic failure."
        }
      ],
      "witness": [
        {
          "field": "status_and_code",
          "detail": "RECORDED AND EVALUATED UNDER `contested`, NOT SCORED. See the block below."
        },
        {
          "field": "correlated_by_request_id",
          "detail": "RECORDED, NOT SCORED. §4.11 asks for correlation \"where the id is available\". Whether an id inside a frame the peer refused AT HASH-VALIDATION TIME — before it had reason to read the data — counts as available is not settled by the pinned text. Asserting it either way would be inventing a requirement."
        },
        {
          "field": "closed_after_answer",
          "detail": "RECORDED, NEVER SCORED — §4.11 makes it the peer's own choice"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "negative_control_truthful_root_hash",
      "kind": "negative-control",
      "given": "a fresh TCP connection, no frames previously sent on it",
      "why": [
        "The SAME hello with the ONE thing under test corrected: a truthful root content_hash. The",
        "peer must ANSWER AFFIRMATIVELY. Without this arm, a peer that refuses everything — or one",
        "that rejects our hello for a reason that has nothing to do with the hash, a malformed",
        "`peer_id`, a `protocols` list it cannot intersect — produces the same observation as a peer",
        "correctly refusing a mis-hashed root, and the probe cannot tell them apart.",
        "",
        "⛔ AN AFFIRMATIVE 2xx IS THE BAR. `any response` would accept the exact refusal that voids",
        "the probe."
      ],
      "step": [
        {
          "op": "send_frame",
          "detail": "the identical hello envelope with a truthful root content_hash"
        },
        {
          "op": "read_frame",
          "detail": "one answer"
        }
      ],
      "accept": [
        {
          "outcome": "hello_answered",
          "status": 200,
          "detail": "EXECUTE_RESPONSE, 2xx"
        }
      ],
      "refuse": [
        {
          "outcome": "control_void",
          "detail": "anything else — the requirement's row becomes SKIP with `peer_attributable: false` and the reason attached"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],

  "contested": {
    "about": "whether the pinned snapshot assigns a (status, code) to a root-entity content_hash mismatch",
    "requirement_file_says": [
      "ECP-R3 `reading`: \"⚠ THE CODE IS STILL NOT PINNED, AND THIS FILE MUST NOT INVENT ONE",
      "(prohibition 2). §4.11's cause table has no root-hash row and arch's ruling says so",
      "deliberately ... ⇒ ANY status and code satisfies this file; the FRAME is what is asserted.\""
    ],
    "this_suite_reads": [
      "The pinned v0.8.2.26 DOES assign one — `400 hash_mismatch` — and the file's premise is",
      "contradicted by §4.11's own text in the same snapshot."
    ],
    "evidence": [
      "(1) §6.5's dispatch chain, verbatim in the pinned snapshot:",
      "      +- Validate root entity hash",
      "      |   -> 400 hash_mismatch, coded frame; MAY then close (§4.11, §5.2a)",
      "    That is a code, assigned to THIS arm, in the declared snapshot. ECP-R3's own",
      "    `Read range` names §6.5.",
      "",
      "(2) §4.11 (0.8.2.26): \"A cause absent from this table is a cause whose code is assigned by",
      "    ITS OWN SECTION, never a refusal exempt from answering.\" §6.5 is that section, and §1.8",
      "    item 1 additionally routes its dispositions to §5.2a.",
      "",
      "(3) ⛔ §4.11's rationale says the omission was NOT deliberate, in terms: \"a corrupted",
      "    root-entity-hash refusal meets the class definition verbatim while appearing in no row,",
      "    and four peers were measured bare-closing or silently dropping it while scoring PASS,",
      "    because AN OMISSION FROM AN ENUMERATION IS INDISTINGUISHABLE FROM A DELIBERATE SCOPE",
      "    LIMIT.\" The requirement file asserts precisely the deliberate scope limit that sentence",
      "    says cannot be inferred from an omission.",
      "",
      "(4) §5.2a corollary 1's 0.8.2.25 scoping does NOT carve the root out. It excludes \"bytes",
      "    that were never hashed\", and DEFINES those in the same sentence: \"a frame that does not",
      "    decode into an Envelope at all is 400 invalid_request\". This probe's frame decodes into",
      "    an Envelope and its bytes were hashed, so the carve-out does not reach it."
    ],
    "why_it_is_not_acted_on_here": [
      "Prohibition 2. A requirement we invented is a requirement nobody agreed to. The scored",
      "verdict stays on the frame obligation — which both readings assert — and the code evaluation",
      "rides alongside as data, keyed to the requirement id, so the architecture seat can adjudicate",
      "a well-posed question instead of a rerun."
    ],
    "routed_as": [
      "(a) a requirement-file defect for this repo: ECP-R3's `reading` should be re-authored against",
      "    §6.5 and §4.11's 0.8.2.26 rationale, and its `conformant` arm gains a (status, code).",
      "(b) a question for the architecture seat: confirm §6.5's assignment is normative for this",
      "    cause, and add the row to §4.11's table so the next reader does not re-derive this."
    ]
  },

  "measured": [
    "First run 2026-09-17 against `entity-core-go` (posture grants=bootstrap-default).",
    "",
    "CONTROL HELD — 200 EXECUTE_RESPONSE to the truthful hello.",
    "PROBE: `bare_close`. The peer closed with no coded frame. §4.11's SECOND named failure.",
    "",
    "⛔ THE CONTESTED CODE QUESTION IS UNDECIDED BY THIS RUN AND MUST NOT BE REPORTED AS DECIDED.",
    "core-go emits NO code on this surface at all, so nothing here distinguishes the two readings.",
    "The disagreement is only decidable against a peer that answers with a code, and no such peer",
    "was run this session."
  ]
}
